{%- comment -%}
  Per-section layout control.

  Companion to pl-scheme: that snippet moves a section's colour tokens, this
  one moves its geometry. Both work the same way — they emit a style block
  scoped to one `#shopify-section-…` that re-points design tokens the CSS is
  already written against, so a merchant changing a slider in the theme editor
  moves the padding, the measure, the heading scale and the corner radius
  together instead of leaving half the section on the old rhythm.

  Nothing here is required. Every value falls back to the value the stylesheet
  already uses, so a section that renders this without setting anything looks
  exactly as it did before. That matters because six of these sections are
  shared with the product page and other templates, whose JSON does not set
  the new keys.

  Usage
    {% render 'pl-layout', id: section.id, s: section.settings %}

  Reads, all optional, from `s`
    pad_top, pad_bottom            desktop padding in px
    pad_top_m, pad_bottom_m        the same on phones (below 750px)
    width                          narrow | normal | wide | full
    align                          left | center
    heading_scale                  percentage applied to display headings
    divider_top, divider_bottom    hairline rules on the section edges
    corners                        square | soft | round
    animate                        false stops the scroll reveal in this section
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- liquid
  assign has_pt = false
  assign has_pb = false
  if s.pad_top != blank or s.pad_top == 0
    assign has_pt = true
  endif
  if s.pad_bottom != blank or s.pad_bottom == 0
    assign has_pb = true
  endif

  case s.width
    when 'narrow'
      assign maxw = '1040px'
    when 'wide'
      assign maxw = '1440px'
    when 'full'
      assign maxw = 'none'
  endcase

  case s.corners
    when 'square'
      assign r_sm = '0px'
      assign r_lg = '0px'
      assign r_pill = '4px'
    when 'round'
      assign r_sm = '22px'
      assign r_lg = '34px'
  endcase

  assign scale = s.heading_scale | default: 100
-%}
{%- comment -%}
  The overlay stylesheet, loaded after pl-styles.css rather than merged into
  it. Two reasons: the base file is 98KB and is edited on the store
  independently, so folding 13KB of new rules into it turns every future
  change into a merge conflict on the one file every page loads; and keeping
  them separate makes it obvious which rules exist to serve these controls.

  Everything in it either re-declares a base rule with the original value as
  its fallback, or styles a class the base file has never heard of.
{%- endcomment -%}
{{ 'pl-layout.css' | asset_url | stylesheet_tag }}
<style>
  #shopify-section-{{ id }} .pl.pl {
    {%- if has_pt %} --sec-pt: {{ s.pad_top }}px;{% endif -%}
    {%- if has_pb %} --sec-pb: {{ s.pad_bottom }}px;{% endif -%}
    {%- if maxw != blank %} --sec-maxw: {{ maxw }};{% endif -%}
    {%- if r_sm != blank %} --radius: {{ r_sm }}; --radius-lg: {{ r_lg }};{% endif -%}
    {%- if r_pill != blank %} --radius-pill: {{ r_pill }};{% endif -%}
    {%- if scale != 100 %} --sec-h-scale: {{ scale | divided_by: 100.0 }};{% endif -%}
  }
  {%- if s.align == 'center' %}
  /* Centre the section's own head and any lead paragraph under it. The grids
     below stay on their own alignment — centring a product row's copy is a
     different decision and has its own control. */
  #shopify-section-{{ id }} .pl .section-head,
  #shopify-section-{{ id }} .pl .cats__head {
    margin-inline: auto;
    text-align: center;
  }
  {%- endif -%}
  {%- if s.divider_top %}
  #shopify-section-{{ id }} .pl > .pl-section,
  #shopify-section-{{ id }} .pl > .pl-hero { border-top: 1px solid var(--sand); }
  {%- endif -%}
  {%- if s.divider_bottom %}
  #shopify-section-{{ id }} .pl > .pl-section,
  #shopify-section-{{ id }} .pl > .pl-hero { border-bottom: 1px solid var(--sand); }
  {%- endif -%}
  {%- if s.animate == false %}
  /* Reveal is opt-out rather than removed from the markup, so turning motion
     off cannot leave an element stuck at opacity 0 if the observer never
     fires. */
  #shopify-section-{{ id }} .pl .reveal { opacity: 1; transform: none; transition: none; }
  {%- endif -%}
  {%- if s.pad_top_m != blank or s.pad_bottom_m != blank %}
  @media (max-width: 749px) {
    #shopify-section-{{ id }} .pl.pl {
      {%- if s.pad_top_m != blank %} --sec-pt: {{ s.pad_top_m }}px;{% endif -%}
      {%- if s.pad_bottom_m != blank %} --sec-pb: {{ s.pad_bottom_m }}px;{% endif -%}
    }
  }
  {%- endif -%}
</style>
